From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niranjana Vishwanathapura <niranjana.vishwanathapura@intel.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Dec 2022 19:54:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915/vm_bind: Support partially mapped vma resource

As persistent vmas can be partialled mapped to an object,
remove restriction which require vma resource sg table to
be just pointer to object's sg table.

Reviewed-by: Matthew Auld <matthew.auld@intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Niranjana Vishwanathapura <niranjana.vishwanathapura@intel.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/i915_vma.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/i915_vma.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/i915_vma.c
index afc192d9931b..2ba53a1bfc20 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/i915_vma.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/i915_vma.c
@@ -2162,8 +2162,7 @@ static struct dma_fence *__i915_vma_unbind_async(struct i915_vma *vma)
 	if (!drm_mm_node_allocated(&vma->node))
 		return NULL;
 
-	if (i915_vma_is_pinned(vma) ||
-	    &vma->obj->mm.rsgt->table != vma->resource->bi.pages)
+	if (i915_vma_is_pinned(vma))
 		return ERR_PTR(-EAGAIN);
 
 	/*

